# Supabase Configuration
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/settings/api
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In-app voice calls (passenger <-> driver)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio is WebRTC peer-to-peer and signalling rides on Supabase Realtime, so
# calls cost nothing per minute. Calls behind symmetric NAT / carrier CGNAT
# (roughly 10-20%) need a TURN relay to connect at all.
#
# There is no working free public TURN any more (the Open Relay Project's is
# dead), so leaving this unset means those calls fail over to the carrier line
# instead of connecting. Two ways to get a relay of your own:
#
#   a) Cloudflare Realtime TURN — free tier, no server to run
#   b) coturn on a ~$5/mo VPS
#
# Either way, set:
#   VITE_TURN_URL=turn:turn.yourdomain.com:3478
#   VITE_TURN_USERNAME=els
#   VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-shared-secret
# VITE_TURN_URL=
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Masked calling (Twilio)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The one ELS voice number both a chauffeur and a guest dial to reach each
# other. Twilio answers it, works out who is calling from their own number,
# and bridges the call — neither party ever sees the other's number, and it
# runs over the carrier line, so it works where the in-app WebRTC call cannot.
#
# Buy a voice-capable UK number in the Twilio console and point its
# "A call comes in" webhook (HTTP POST) at:
#   https://<project>.supabase.co/functions/v1/twilio-voice
#
# The function needs TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN and TWILIO_VOICE_NUMBER set as Supabase
# secrets, and must be deployed with --no-verify-jwt. See
# supabase/functions/twilio-voice/index.ts in the els-elite repo.
#
# Leave this unset and the apps fall back to their previous behaviour: the
# in-app call only, with Operations as the backstop.
# VITE_ELS_CALL_NUMBER=+44...
